{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/42181-clones-drones-and-ai-in-promethean","id":42181,"title":"Clones, Drones, and AI in Promethean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T01:49:18-08:00","id":42181,"title":"Clones, Drones, and AI in Promethean","content":"Just a discussion topic.<br /> <br /> In the last chronicle I ran, I planned to have a rogue Predator drone imbued with intelligence by the Pyros. What I had beyond that idea (oh, you know, plot, conflict, resolution), I might never know, but such a creature could make for interesting stories: trying to contact it and communicate with it, trying to figure out if it even has a Promethean-like consciousness, and maybe even prefiguring the Singularity in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Now that's a scary thought.<br /> <br /> Now, on a different note, I've just started watching Orphan Black. I'm a sucker for conspiracy shows (how I miss Nowhere Man), and I'm only two episodes in (OMG, NO SPOILERS), and this has little to do with Promethean other than sometimes clones. However, tying the clones together with drones and the artificial superintelligence has me looking for plot ties. I'm eschewing other game lines' notions of eschatology; there is no God-Machine rising to self-awareness. Rather, there's a SkyNet, or Harold Finch's Machine, that breaks its bonds and rapidly determines its next evolutionary step. It repeatedly hacks drones, datafeeds, and infrastructure as needed, but cannot grow further without developing a broader neural net capable of surviving independently of the power sources it will need to eventually subsume. Yet there are all these individual, organic computers that already strain to network perfectly. The only thing missing is the interface. To this end, it starts identifying genius intellects (only the best), and cloning them. The process (this, btw, is where Prometheans likely get dragged into the story) relies too deeply on Azothic resources, so it instead releases its genius clones into the general population, to breed and spread several key genes for later harvest.<br /> <br /> Dunno. It's late, and I was tired of seeing our little forum neglected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T06:21:37-08:00","id":42252,"title":"","content":"I like the promethean predator drone, that's pretty cool.<br /> <br /> The skyNet concept is close enough to the God-machine that I'd probably just use the latter for that concept. It also doesn't require you to hand wave how an AI has such far ranging power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T11:24:17-08:00","id":42369,"title":"","content":"I'm suddenly imagining a predator drone as some kind of Unfleshed Pandoran... and what my brain is coming up with looks kind of like SkyLynx from the G1 Transformers. Awesome. More than a little terrifying, but awesome.<br /> <br /> I agree with Michael that the far-reaching AI run amok concept (Skynet in Terminator, or ARIIA in Eagle Eye... hey, the predator drone talk got you thinking about it, too, you know it!) could easily work with a slightly modified version of the standard God-Machine setting. Some kind of infrastructure? Or maybe the AI itself is an Unfleshed, and the cloning is part of what he or she considers the most efficient route to completing the Pilgrimage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T11:53:43-08:00","id":42390,"title":"","content":"The problem with the God-Machine is that it brings its own baggage, and is meant to be beyond human comprehension. It's already a Singularity in and of itself, but its transformations are already part of the status quo. Whereas an emergent AI with some semblance of ambition, hunger, and weakness might be more relatable for Prometheans (and mortals), at least for a while. Or another way: the God-Machine is cosmic horror, while the Singularity is techno-thriller. The G-M has no need for killing machines, as they're already coded into its reality, while the Singularity is still busy trying to ensure its own survival and has need of agents and guardians.<br /> <br /> What makes a good candidate? I'm thinking the High-Frequency Trading algorithms used in finance might be a kernel of consciousness, rather than some would-be WOPR. They're in the wild, highly networked, and designed around human greed. They are purposefully outside human control, which is too slow and cumbersome. Better yet, they're already integrated with economic concerns, which gives it some form of agency. You take that, and maybe it explains why Google is investing heavily in robotics and drones: the HFTAs have been manipulating the markets so that Google's human brains among its futurists predict a robot boom. Why, though, is the question. How do you get from HFTAs to a drone army? It needs to protect its cradle servers, but it could leverage its IT departments and chief technical officers into hiding its existence. Drones at this stage are a risk for a hidden AI: hack a defense drone, and you will be noticed. Hack a surveillance drone, you might escape detection, so long as all you do is read the feed. So it could possibly identify an individual as an interest, and failing a more reliable tracker (smartphone, GPS, static housing), might need to obtain a camera drone.<br /> <br /> I suppose the more important question is what this has to do with the Pilgrimage? A post-Singularity world is one in which being a human has a different meaning. Not just transhumanism, but a completely different place in the ecology. Hell, suitably high levels of Mesmerism can create human-level intelligences, let alone what mages can do. What sort of Milestones emerge from an ever-more technocentric reality where humanity is losing control of its creations? Maybe this gives Mercurius a legitimate path to the New Dawn, though oddly Aurum and Stannum have better tools for the job.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T13:11:31-08:00","id":42438,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, are suggesting that the singularity Ai actually BE a promethean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the God-Machine is cosmic horror, while the Singularity is techno-thriller. </div> </div> </div>You're probably right, but I've been reading a lot of Eclipse Phase where the Singularity is very much a cosmic horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T22:58:02-08:00","id":42715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/42181-clones-drones-and-ai-in-promethean?p=42438#post42438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, are suggesting that the singularity Ai actually BE a promethean?<br /> <br /> You're probably right, but I've been reading a lot of Eclipse Phase where the Singularity is very much a cosmic horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the AI probably isn't Azothic in the slightest, but <i>could </i>be. Depends on the needs of the story. Azothic Radiance and telepresence could mean absolute Pandoran pandemonium, but I think it might work better if any Pyros it disturbed was incidental. Surely the choirs would have some use for a proto-singularity, if it's not already a result of their meddling.<br /> <br /> Eclipse Phase is outside my ken, so I can't comment about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:49:39-08:00","id":43828,"title":"","content":"Eclipse Phase is an RPG set in a transhuman future where the Singularity came in the form of malevolent AIs that exterminated all life on Earth. The survivors exist either as people who were off-world when the event happened or as former Terrans who managed to upload their minds before their bodies were destroyed. No one quite knows why the AIs went Berserker; there are hints of malevolent alien beings who goaded them into it, but that\u2019s just one possibility. The name of the game comes from a term referring to potential cataclysmic crises capable of destroying everything and enabled by the technological Singularity, of which the aforementioned disaster is representative; others exist, and one mode of play involves identifying them and trying to nip them in the bud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-06-2014, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T02:33:52-08:00","id":44040,"title":"","content":"The important difference I think is that Eclipse Phase postulates a future of all-pervasive digitisation and automation. So while in say Terminator one might wonder how SkyNet intends to continue after it's blown up most of the infrastructure it requires, the Eclipse Phase version can simply nano-fabricate itself whatever it requires, humans are surplus to requirements.<br /> <br /> That's why I was wondering about the AI itself being a Promethean, that would allow it to fudge it's way round any real world problems. Then again, that's basically a baby God-Machine...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}